# auto columns of a Table and of a Grid (reference/components/table.md#column-widths). Page area of 260 × 160 from
# (20, 20). Every cell holds a block of a fixed width, which is its narrowest and natural width.
#
# t1: auto auto with blocks of 20 and 60. 180 left over, shared in proportion to the natural widths (1/4 and 3/4):
#   columns of 65 and 195.
# g: the same columns in a Grid, which shares the 180 in equal parts: 110 and 150.
# t2: 40 auto auto with a gap of 10 and blocks of 10 and 30. 240 for the tracks; 40 fixed, and the 160 left over go
#   1/4 and 3/4 to the auto ones: 50 and 150, at x = 70 and 130.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 300
		Height: 200
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
		For element: Block
			Box:
				Height: 20
				Background: #B5D4F4
	Section:
		Table:
			Id: t1
			Column sizes: auto auto
			Body:
				Row:
					Cell:
						Id: t1a
						Block:
							Box:
								Width: 20
					Cell:
						Id: t1b
						Block:
							Box:
								Width: 60
		Grid:
			Id: g
			Column sizes: auto auto
			Area:
				Block:
					Id: g1
					Box:
						Width: 20
			Area:
				Block:
					Id: g2
					Box:
						Width: 60
		Table:
			Id: t2
			Column sizes: 40 auto auto
			Gap: 10
			Body:
				Row:
					Cell:
						Id: t2a
						Block:
							Box:
								Width: 40
					Cell:
						Id: t2b
						Block:
							Box:
								Width: 10
					Cell:
						Id: t2c
						Block:
							Box:
								Width: 30
